# Copy to .env (gitignored) and adjust for your machine.
# Read by `docker compose` and by a local run (`python -m kio2.main`).

# Host-side folder mounted read-only into the KIO2 container at /workspace —
# see the `volumes:` comment in docker-compose.yml. Put or point at the code
# you want KIO2 to trace, then reference it via its /workspace/... path in
# target_script / working_directory (e.g. from the /playground page).
#
# Defaults to ./workspace (in this repo) when unset. A sibling checkout also
# works, e.g.:
# KIO2_WORKSPACE=../Trace/test-codes

# Local run only: where recorded traces (kio2_<id>.xml) are written, and the only
# directory a trace reference may point into. Defaults to the system temporary
# directory (on Windows %LOCALAPPDATA%\Temp). Use an absolute path. KIO2 does not
# delete traces, so clean this folder yourself. Inside the container traces stay
# in the container's /tmp; open them with GET /traces/<token> either way.
# KIO2_TRACE_DIR=E:/kio2-traces

# Longest recording, in seconds: over POST /execute (synchronous) and over
# POST /jobs (the job contract KIO1 dispatches with).
# KIO2_TRACE_BUDGET=45
# KIO2_JOB_TRACE_BUDGET=180

# The /playground page can run edited or pasted code. That code is executed on
# this machine and the service has no authentication, so it is off by default.
# Enable it only on a machine you trust, e.g. for a local demo.
# KIO2_PLAYGROUND_SNIPPETS=1
